   "variant_id": "h33-h33-2-b2-CONCENTRATIONphys10-20261024-b93a4cf8",
   "hypothesis": "Where magnetic horizontal gradient, isostatic-gravity slope and detrended-elevation slope are jointly high, the crust is more intensely broken per km^2, so truth density per km^2 is high there. This prior is built only from physics, so unlike the catalogue prior it cannot inherit mapping effort or exposure bias.",
   "mechanism": "Same fixed-S budget trade as catd10, with the block prior replaced by the 0.40 pct(tmi_hg) + 0.35 pct(iso_grav_anom_slope) + 0.25 pct(det_elev_slope) mix smoothed to 1 km. Differences ONLY which blocks are donors and receivers: same count, same mass, same spacing floor, same catalogue clearance.",
   "non_fault_mimic": "The same bands respond to non-tectonic contrasts: Tertiary volcanic flow margins, caldera ring fractures, pluton contacts, and lithologic scarps in resistant tuff. Because the physics mix is also what the H19-5 ridge mask was built to track, the implied redistribution is the mildest of the three variants.",
